d gate samples and ticket-store sizing data already captured in the parent/children.'","Parent witted-invisible-roan comment: 'The campaign found the governing variable is concurrency, not store size or gate phase: 69 MB base, ~295 MB per concurrent whole-store read before the fix and ~84 MB after.'","Parent comment: 'change 2685 merged ... ~295 MB -> ~84 MB per concurrent whole-store read (3.5x)'","Parent GATE_PEAK_RSS table: completion_verifier 418-441 MiB with peak_delta_bytes 0 — 'a data point AGAINST gate RSS scaling with ticket size'"],"finding":"The plan re-derives an RSS-vs-ticket-size conclusion from recorded gate samples without reconciling with the parent RCA, which already established the governing variable is CONCURRENCY (RSS = 69MB + K x 295MB), refuted ticket-size scaling (completion_verifier 416-441MB with peak_delta_bytes ~0), and CHANGED the underlying per-read memory constant via merged change 2685 (~295MB -> ~84MB per concurrent read). Mixing pre- and post-2685 GATE_PEAK_RSS markers / container RSS windows would derive a capacity number from a defect that no longer exists.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f649f08e8ba144729","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 4 / AC3","norm_id":"nfd952ddb40c84b8d","priority":0.4467,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer harvests GATE_PEAK_RSS markers and container RSS windows spanning before and after 2685's deploy and reports a single blended peak/scaling number, overstating current per-read cost by up to ~3.5x.","The capacity conclusion is framed around ticket size when the parent already showed concurrency is the driver, producing a mem_limit/instance recommendation keyed on the wrong variable."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In step 4, state the derivation uses only post-2685-deploy samples, reconciles with the parent's RSS = 69MB + K x 84MB model, and reports RSS-vs-concurrency (K) as the primary axis with ticket-size as the already-refuted 